    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "DSA_SIGNALS",
      "narration": "Your giveaway word is shortest, and it's almost always literally in the question. Minimum steps, or fewest moves, which is the same thing wearing a different hat. Level order, when a tree has to be read row by row. Nearest, or closest, which means distance again. But if the edges have different weights, plain breadth-first search is wrong and you want Dijkstra instead. And if you only need to know whether a path exists at all, depth-first is cheaper. Shortest is the word. Everything else follows from it.",
      "durationFrames": 875,
      "timingSource": "tts",
