    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "DSA_SIGNALS",
      "narration": "Here's what to remember when you're tired and under pressure. Take from the front and you've breadth-first search, which fans out in rings and gives you shortest. Take from the back and you've depth-first search, which dives down one branch. Popleft is BFS. Pop is DFS. And BFS costs memory, because a wide ring is a big queue. Same code, one word different, completely different answer, and that trade is worth naming before anybody asks you for it.",
      "durationFrames": 820,
      "timingSource": "tts",
